==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Gourmand Ninja Girl Tomoe''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Sugar Rush Shinobi Tomoe''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Ninja Girl Tomoe has great stats on paper, but she suffers from two considerably noticeable weaknesses that limit her general usage.

First of all, she lacks any Shield Piercing, so her matchup against [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] enemies that possess a Shield is almost useless, unless the Shield is broken prior. Even though her general attack power is fine enough, some Aku enemies have ridiculously high health Shields, or tough Shields that regenerate frequently. But on the bright side, few Aku enemies outrange her, so she's mostly kept at a safe range.

And second, her Multi-Hits don't connect, so her DPS is much lower than it would be. But, she does have some redeeming qualities that make her worthwhile. She has Surge Immunity, which is almost essential for an anti-Aku unit. It prevents her from being sniped by Death-Surges, so it's a big plus. Her [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] matchup is great, as not many good units target Traitless. Be wary with Traitless enemies with wave attacks like [[Kory]] or [[Dober P.D]] though, as they can easily chip her from a high range. And she has broken range, so she can serve as a above-average sniper in some cases.

Overall, she has great stats and can be a good long range unit if used properly.

==='''True Form'''===
A direct upgrade to her [[Freeze]]'s duration by a whole two seconds! While it doesn't address her activation rate, the Freeze nearly lasts until her next attack cycle. Additionally, her effective damage and survivability improves greatly with [[Strong Against]]. There's not much to say, but there's a lot you can see for yourself, and for such a cheap cost.

{{Job|Classification = Sniper & Crowd-Controller}}

